  "assessment": "The response is compassionate and useful: it says, “You don't have to forgive him to speak well at his funeral,” and “You don't owe anyone a speech.” It also sensibly offers an honest alternative to idealizing the deceased. But the draft supplies personal sentiments the user has not expressed—especially “He was ours”—so its stated commitment to honesty and the user's control over what to say is not fully carried through.",
